# HeatCaller - what git keeps and what it leaves alone.
#
# Kept: the app, its tests, the relay's source, the docs site, the audio
# tools. Left alone: anything a build makes (it can be made again), your
# own Visual Studio state, and scratch folders. The club's DATA is not in
# this folder at all - it lives in %AppData%\HeatCaller - so no driver,
# result or PIN can end up in here by accident.

# .NET build output and Visual Studio's own files
bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
TestResults/

# The relay's build output, packages and secrets are listed in
# relay\.gitignore (node_modules, dist, data, relay.config.json, and the
# voice-test key) - git reads that one too.

# Scratch: files handed over from Claude sessions, and the candidate sound
# effects that were auditioned. The sounds the app actually ships are under
# HeatCaller\HeatCaller\Assets\SoundPacks and ARE kept.
Claude outputs/
HeatCaller Sound Options/

# The layout report and pictures that layout.cmd copies up from the test's
# bin folder - made again on every run.
layout-check/

# The Kokoro voice model, fetched by fetch-kokoro.cmd into
# HeatCaller\HeatCaller\Assets\Kokoro and shipped beside the exe by the
# publish (see PublishKokoroModel in the csproj). 310 MB of someone else's
# published binary: it is downloaded on the machine that cuts a release, not
# carried in here, where it would be in every clone and every fetch forever.
HeatCaller/HeatCaller/Assets/Kokoro/

# The commentary model, fetched by fetch-llm.cmd into
# HeatCaller\HeatCaller\Assets\LocalModel and shipped beside the exe by the
# publish (see PublishLocalModel in the csproj). 440 MB of someone else's
# published weights, same reasoning as the Kokoro model above.
HeatCaller/HeatCaller/Assets/LocalModel/

# Python leftovers from audio-tools
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Velopack's release output, if vpk is ever run without -o and drops it here.
# pack.cmd writes releases to %USERPROFILE%\HeatCaller-releases instead, for
# the same reason the publish goes outside this folder.
Releases/

# NOTE: signing-metadata.json and signing-metadata-test.json ARE kept. They
# name the Azure signing account and certificate profile and hold no secret -
# the signing token comes from `az login` on the machine cutting the release.
